netfilter: nft_set_pipapo: fix null deref for empty set

jira KERNEL-1646
cve CVE-2025-39867
Rebuild_History Non-Buildable kernel-5.14.0-687.51.1.el9_8
commit-author Florian Westphal <fw@strlen.de>
commit 30c1d25b9870d551be42535067d5481668b5e6f3
Empty-Commit: Cherry-Pick Conflicts during history rebuild.
Will be included in final tarball splat. Ref for failed cherry-pick at:
ciq/ciq_backports/kernel-5.14.0-687.51.1.el9_8/30c1d25b.failed

Blamed commit broke the check for a null scratch map:
  -  if (unlikely(!m || !*raw_cpu_ptr(m->scratch)))
  +  if (unlikely(!raw_cpu_ptr(m->scratch)))

This should have been "if (!*raw_ ...)".
Use the pattern of the avx2 version which is more readable.

This can only be reproduced if avx2 support isn't available.

Fixes: d8d871a35ca9 ("netfilter: nft_set_pipapo: merge pipapo_get/lookup")
	Signed-off-by: Florian Westphal <fw@strlen.de>
(cherry picked from commit 30c1d25b9870d551be42535067d5481668b5e6f3)
	Signed-off-by: Jonathan Maple <jmaple@ciq.com>

